# STIG CD16-00-004600: PostgreSQL must separate user functionality (including user 
# STIG ID: V-261898 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-004600-user-separation-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-004600: PostgreSQL must separate user functionality (including user interface services) `
    description `PostgreSQL must separate user functionality (including user interface services) from database management functionality.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-004600,NIST-800-53:SC-2`
    control_objective `SC-2`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA STIG guidance for CD16-00-004600.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_SC_2 `This control is validated by checking the required PostgreSQL configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT pg_query
        query `role_attributes`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE query_check
        found boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN pg_catalog_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF query_check
            OBJECT_REF pg_query
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
